  "prefLabel": "Plc 1903.01 Qualifications for Initial Doula Certification",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1903.01 Qualifications for Initial Doula Certification. To qualify for certification as a doula, an individual shall:\n\n(a) Be of good moral character, as demonstrated by the responses on the application to the questions listed in Plc 304.03(e) and any explanation(s) provided pursuant to Plc 304.04(a); and\n\n(b) Have received training and experience in the core competencies identified in Plc 1903.02.\n\nSource. #14429, eff 1-16-26, EXPIRES 1-16-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1900.html"
